    "# Ecosystem\n",
    "\t1. Spark Core: Provides the execution engine, DAG scheduling, memory management, fault tolerance, and integration with cluster managers.(Cluster managers = Standalone, YARN, Kubernetes, Mesos)\n",
    "\t2. Spark SQL: Provides a unified engine for structured data processing using SQL, DataFrames, and Datasets.(Note: Spark SQL is not just SQL; it powers DataFrames, Datasets, and Structured Streaming.)\n",
    "\t3. Spark ML (formerly MLlib): Scalable machine learning using DataFrame-based APIs.\n",
    "\t4. Spark Structured Streaming: Real-time stream processing using DataFrames/Datasets with event-time semantics.\n",
    "    5. GraphX: Graph processing library available only in Scala.\n",
    "\n",
    "# Languages:\n",
    "    1. Python(Pyspark)\n",
    "    2. SQL(Spark SQL)\n",
    "    3. Java\n",
    "    4. Scala (Native language of Spark)\n",
    "    5. R(SparkR)\n"
