    "### Adaptive Query Plan(AQE)\n",
    "- spark.conf.set(\"spark.sql.adaptive.enabled\")\n",
    "- AQE is query re-optimization that occurs during query execution. It allows Spark to make runtime decisions to improve performance based on the actual data statistics.(Runtime query optimization based on actual data)\n",
    "\n",
    "######** Key Features**\n",
    "- Dynamically switch join strategies: For example, it can convert a sort-merge join into a broadcast join if one side of the join is small.\n",
    "- Dynamically coalesce partitions: Reduces the number of small shuffle partitions to improve efficiency.\n",
    "- Handle skewed data dynamically: Detects skew in join keys and splits or mitigates skewed partitions.\n",
    "- Detect and propagate empty results: Optimizes queries by skipping unnecessary computation if a dataset or partition is empty.\n",
    "\n",
    "![](Images/ApacheSpark/AQE1.png)\n",
    "![](Images/ApacheSpark/AQE2.png)\n",
    "![](Images/ApacheSpark/AQE3.png)\n",
    "![](Images/ApacheSpark/AQE4.png)\n",
    "![](Images/ApacheSpark/AQE5.png)"
   ]
