   "source": [
    "# Apache Spark vs MapReduce\n",
    "\n",
    "**MapReduce:** The Map phase is responsible for distributing the data across machines, and the Reduce phase gathers and aggregates the results from those machines.\n",
    "  **Drawback:** Intermediate results (joins, aggregations, etc.) are written to disk. Every time the system needs to read or fetch this data from disk for further processing, it takes additional time because of disk I/O operations.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Apache Spark:** It processes data mainly in memory, so there is no need to write intermediate results to disk. This makes processing much faster compared to MapReduce.\n",
    "  **Features:**\n",
    "  In-Memory Computation,\n",
    "  Lazy Evaluation,\n",
    "  Fault Tolerant,\n",
    "  Partitioning,\n",
    "  Streaming and Batch Processing using same API(Code)"
   ]
  },
