   "source": [
    "### DAG Scheduler\n",
    "In Apache Spark, DAG stands for Directed Acyclic Graph. It is a fundamental concept used by Spark’s execution engine to represent the flow of operations in a data processing job and to schedule the execution as jobs, stages, and tasks.\n",
    "![](Images/ApacheSpark/DAG.png)\n",
    "\n",
    "![](Images/ApacheSpark/DAG%20Flow.png)\n",
    "\n",
    "##### Why DAGs are Important?\n",
    "-   **Execution Planning and Scheduling:** Spark uses the DAG to intelligently break down a complex job into stages and tasks. This helps it optimize how to compute results efficiently across a cluster of computers.\n",
    "-   **Understand Job Execution:** The DAG offers a bird's-eye view of your Spark job's logical structure, making it easier to understand the flow of your data transformations.\n",
    "-   **Debugging:** If your Spark job encounters issues, you can often use the DAG to pinpoint where failures might be occurring.\n",
    "![](Images/ApacheSpark/DAG%20Ex.png)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "application/vnd.databricks.v1+cell": {
     "cellMetadata": {
