   "source": [
    "# Spark Session\n",
    "A Spark Session is the entry point to work with Apache Spark. It is the main object you use to interact with Spark for reading data, running transformations, and executing queries.\n",
    "\n",
    "\uD83D\uDD39 Why it exists\n",
    "\n",
    "Before Spark 2.0, you had multiple contexts:\n",
    "SQLContext\n",
    "HiveContext\n",
    "SparkContext\n",
    "\uD83D\uDC49 Now, SparkSession combines all of them into one.\n",
    "\n",
    "\uD83D\uDD39 What it provides\n",
    "\n",
    "With a SparkSession, you can:\n",
    "\n",
    "Read data (CSV, Parquet, Delta, etc.)\n",
    "Create DataFrames\n",
    "Run SQL queries\n",
    "Access Spark configuration\n",
    "Manage catalogs (tables, databases)"
