   "source": [
    "### Tungsten\n",
    "  Tungsten is Spark’s execution engine that generates optimized Java bytecode and uses off-heap, binary memory layouts to execute tasks with near bare-metal efficiency.\n",
    "\uD83D\uDCCC Tungsten does NOT plan queries — it executes them efficiently.\n",
    "![](Images/ApacheSpark/Tungsten.png)\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Core Components of Tungsten\n",
    "##### 1. Whole-Stage Code Generation (Most Important)\n",
    "######**Problem without Tungsten:**\n",
    "- Each operator (filter, project, join) runs as a separate iterator\n",
    "- Too many virtual function calls\n",
    "- Too many Java objects\n",
    "- CPU pipeline stalls\n",
    "\n",
    "######**What Tungsten does:**\n",
    "- Fuses multiple operators into a single Java method\n",
    "- Generates Java bytecode at runtime\n",
    "- Compiles it using Janino\n",
    "- Executes as a tight while loop\n",
    "\n",
    "\uD83D\uDCCC This dramatically reduces:\n",
    "- Function call overhead\n",
    "- Object creation\n",
    "- Branch misprediction\n",
    "![](Images/ApacheSpark/WholestageCodeGen.png)\n",
    "\n",
    "##### 2. UnsafeRow (Binary Row Format)\n",
    "###### **Before Tungsten:**\n",
    "- Rows stored as Java objects\n",
    "- High GC overhead\n",
    "- Poor cache locality\n",
    "\n",
    "###### **With Tungsten:**\n",
    "- Rows stored in compact binary format\n",
    "- Fixed-width fields + variable-length area\n",
    "- Accessed via raw memory offsets\n",
    "\n",
    "\uD83D\uDCCC Benefits:\n",
    "- Less memory\n",
    "- Faster comparisons\n",
    "- Better CPU cache usage\n",
    "\n",
    "##### 3. Off-Heap Memory Management\n",
    "###### **Problem:**\n",
    "- JVM heap → frequent GC pauses\n",
    "- Large shuffles cause GC pressure\n",
    "\n",
    "##### **Tungsten solution:**\n",
    "- Uses off-heap memory\n",
    "- Manages memory manually\n",
    "- Reduces GC overhead\n",
    "\n",
    "\uD83D\uDCCC Especially important for:\n",
    "- Shuffles\n",
    "- Sorts\n",
    "- Aggregations\n",
    "\n",
    "##### 4. Cache-Friendly Data Structures\n",
    "###### **Tungsten designs structures to:**\n",
    "- Fit CPU cache lines\n",
    "- Enable SIMD optimizations\n",
    "- Minimize pointer chasing\n",
    "\n",
    "Examples:\n",
    "- Binary formats\n",
    "- Contiguous memory layouts\n",
    "\n",
    "##### 5. Efficient Shuffle, Sort & Aggregation\n",
    "###### **Tungsten optimizes:**\n",
    "- Hash aggregation\n",
    "- Sort-based aggregation\n",
    "- Shuffle spill handling\n",
    "\n",
    "Uses:\n",
    "- Fewer objects\n",
    "- Better memory reuse\n",
    "- Faster serialization"
   ]
  },
