   "source": [
    "## Deployment Modes (Synapse / Fabric Context)\n",
    "\n",
    "- Client Mode: The driver runs on the compute attached to your notebook/session (managed by Synapse/Fabric). You don’t directly manage the driver, but it behaves like client mode where execution is tied to your session. Mainly used during development and interactive analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Cluster Mode: The driver runs fully managed within the platform’s compute infrastructure. This is abstracted from the user, but effectively behaves like cluster mode where execution is independent of your session. Preferred for production pipelines and scheduled jobs.\n",
    "\n",
    "###### Key understanding (important in your project):\n",
    "- In Synapse/Fabric, you don’t explicitly choose client vs cluster mode\n",
    "- The platform manages the driver internally\n",
    "###### For:\n",
    "- Notebooks → behaves like client mode\n",
    "- Pipelines / scheduled jobs → behaves like cluster mode\n",
    "###### Simple way to remember:\n",
    "- Notebook run → Session dependent\n",
    "- Pipeline run → Session independent (production safe)\n",
    "\n",
    "###### How it actually works:\n",
    "#######\uD83D\uDFE2 Notebooks\n",
    "- Behave like client mode\n",
    "- Execution is tied to your session\n",
    "- If session stops → job may stop\n",
    "#######\uD83D\uDD35 Pipelines / Scheduled jobs\n",
    "- Behave like cluster mode\n",
    "- Run independently of your session\n",
    "- Production-safe\n",
    "###### Key point:\n",
    "\n",
    "- \uD83D\uDC49 Both modes are abstracted\n",
    "- \uD83D\uDC49 Internally everything runs on cluster compute\n",
    "- \uD83D\uDC49 But behavior differs based on how you trigger the job\n",
    "\n",
    "###### Better statement you can use:\n",
    "\n",
    "“In Synapse and Fabric, Spark execution is managed by the platform. Notebooks behave like client mode, while pipelines behave like cluster mode, though internally everything runs on cluster infrastructure.”\n",
    "\n",
    "###### Simple memory trick:\n",
    "- Notebook → interactive → client-like\n",
    "- Pipeline → independent → cluster-like"
   ]
  },
