    "# Lazy Evaluation and Action\n",
    "Lazy evaluation means that transformations on data (like map, filter, join) are not executed immediately. Instead, Spark records these transformations as a logical execution plan (DAG – Directed Acyclic Graph). The actual computation only happens when an action (like collect, count, save) is called, allowing Spark to optimize execution, reduce unnecessary computations, and improve performance.\n",
    "![](Images/ApacheSpark/LazyEvaluation&Action.png)"
